A bot, in the context of computing, is a software application designed to perform automated tasks. These tasks can range from simple, like answering frequently asked questions, to complex, such as setting alarms or reminders, making calculations, or even engaging in simulated conversations (as in the case of chatbots). Bots can operate on various platforms, including websites, apps, and messaging services. They are often used to improve efficiency, save time, and enhance user experience.
